  "worked_solution": "The number is *positive* because it is to the *right* of zero.\n\nThe absolute value of the number is $\\frac{21}{4},$ so the distance between that number and zero on a number line is $\\frac{21}{4}.$ \n\nThe positive number at a distance of $\\frac{21}{4}$ from zero is $\\frac{21}{4}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14145654/assets/6c86e406964238ba196b7f79ef731a618efb46748d9d22b79ff27dba2cf0069b.png)",
